From: millia ampora <198710911+dappermint@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: unregister from the server when an msync wait bails
 out on contention

Ported for CrossOver 26.3 from dappermint/winecx commit
9be392b3b4b845a87b8b7a4d98fbcd8ded682a04 (branch wine1119),
code unchanged. A downstream msync fix, not a
WineHQ backport: WineHQ has no msync. Runs only when WINEMSYNC is set.

the spin loop returns STATUS_PENDING as soon as one of the objects becomes
contended, but it only decremented multiple_waiters locally and never sent
the unregister message, so the tid stayed registered on every object in the
set. it also skipped the alert object's counter, which then never falls back
to zero and forces a mach send on every apc delivery for the rest of the
thread's life.

server_remove_wait already does both decrements and sends the message, and
it is ordered behind the register we just sent on the same mach port.
---
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/msync.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/msync.c
@@ -377,15 +377,7 @@
     {
         if (check_shm_contention( objs_shm, alert_obj_shm, count, tid ))
         {
-            int i;
-            for (i = 0; i < count; i++)
-            {
-                struct event *obj = (struct event *)objs_shm[i];
-
-                int refs = __atomic_sub_fetch( &obj->multiple_waiters, 1, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST);
-                if (refs < 0)
-                    __atomic_store_n( &obj->multiple_waiters, 0, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST);
-            }
+            server_remove_wait( msgh_id, objs, objs_shm, alert_obj, alert_obj_shm, count );
             return STATUS_PENDING;
         }
     }
